#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:155
msgid "Settings of one form"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:159
msgid "A form follows the site-wide settings until you change something on its screen. The more specific setting wins: site, then form, then the form action in the Elementor editor, then routing rules."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:160
msgid "You do not have to add an action to the form. The action \"Forms Notifier\" in the editor is for people who prefer to set a form up there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:161
msgid "Rules are read from top to bottom. A rule can add receivers, replace them, keep only some channels or stop all notifications, depending on what was entered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:162
msgid "For translations of one page link the forms: one form keeps the settings and every text can have a version per language."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:167
#: assets/js/miniapp/app.js:817
msgid "Saved submissions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:171
msgid "Submissions are saved on this site, with their files, unless you switch saving off in the general settings. Passwords and fields marked as sensitive are never saved."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:172
msgid "If Elementor Pro collected submissions earlier, the Import button copies them. Nobody is notified and nothing is imported twice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:173
msgid "How long data is kept is set under Settings, Privacy and data. The personal data tools of WordPress include submissions, files and messages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:178
msgid "Channels and receivers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:182
msgid "A channel is a way to send: Telegram, Bale, SMS, WhatsApp, email, webhooks and others. Receivers are the people, groups or addresses behind it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:183
msgid "A channel is ready when its lamp is green. Amber means something is missing; the screen of the channel says what."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:184
msgid "Tokens and passwords are stored encrypted and never shown again. They can also be set as constants in wp-config.php; the name of the constant is shown next to a locked field."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpContent.php:185
msgid "A receiver can have its own message language and can be limited to submissions in some languages."
msgstr ""

